00:07:38.314 --> 00:07:39.778
And the way that it went down

00:07:39.778 --> 00:07:40.294
is this.

00:07:40.294 --> 00:07:42.110
Brian came in, and felt like

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.230
there's this one problem that he

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.512
had which is his pants didn't fit.

00:07:46.512 --> 00:07:47.932
And so he did one of these

00:07:47.932 --> 00:07:49.997
projects, I can't remember what

00:07:49.997 --> 00:07:51.786
they're called, G 300.

00:07:51.786 --> 00:07:52.571
He used to be call them

00:07:52.571 --> 00:07:53.368
the 300 project.

00:07:53.368 --> 00:07:55.120
And he went out, and he got this

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.155
survey with all of our classmates.

00:07:57.155 --> 00:08:00.778
And the basic insights were Guys

00:08:00.778 --> 00:08:03.230
wear jeans because khaki pants and

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.603
wool pants don't fit that well.

00:08:05.603 --> 00:08:06.161
So that was

00:08:06.161 --> 00:08:07.526
like insight number one.

00:08:07.526 --> 00:08:09.381
And insight number two was,

00:08:09.381 --> 00:08:11.857
guys don't like shopping in stores.

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:14.091
And then insight number three was

00:08:14.091 --> 00:08:16.164
that J Crew and Banana Republic

00:08:16.164 --> 00:08:17.927
were the two main places.

00:08:17.927 --> 00:08:19.856
So his view about men's pants

00:08:19.856 --> 00:08:22.171
